Problem 1: Control-M job failed during a Snowflake load

Symptom: The COPY INTO job failed with "Numeric value 'N/A' is not recognized" or "number of columns in file does not match."

-- What failed, in which file, at which line?
SELECT file_name, status, first_error_message, first_error_line_number
FROM TABLE(INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COPY_HISTORY(
  TABLE_NAME => 'ORDERS',
  START_TIME => DATEADD(hours, -24, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP())));

-- Dry-run the file to see all bad rows
COPY INTO orders FROM @my_stage/orders_2026-09-30.csv
FILE_FORMAT = (FORMAT_NAME = my_csv)
VALIDATION_MODE = RETURN_ERRORS;

Problem 2: Query that used to take 2 minutes now takes 40

SELECT query_id, query_text, total_elapsed_time/1000 AS secs,
       bytes_spilled_to_local_storage, bytes_spilled_to_remote_storage,
       partitions_scanned, partitions_total, queued_overload_time
FROM SNOWFLAKE.ACCOUNT_USAGE.QUERY_HISTORY

Spilling to disk	Warehouse too small for the data	Bigger warehouse, or reduce data earlier
Partitions scanned ≈ total	No pruning	Filter on the clustering/date column, consider clustering key
High queued time	Too many queries on one warehouse	Separate warehouse or multi-cluster
Exploding join	Duplicate join keys	Dedupe first, check join condition

Problem 3: Duplicates appeared after a job rerun
SELECT order_id, COUNT(*) FROM orders GROUP BY order_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;
I make loads idempotent using MERGE or delete-and-insert by batch date, so any rerun gives the same result

Problem 4: Someone ran an UPDATE/DELETE without a WHERE clause
SELECT * FROM orders AT(OFFSET => -60*30);
CREATE TABLE orders_restored CLONE orders AT(OFFSET => -60*30);
